  "_commit": {
    "id": "e1ea79ac6374bcc7e0bb68eb1542cf954a2f9899",
    "author": "Ossama Edbali <ossedb@gmail.com>",
    "committer": "Ossama Edbali <ossedb@gmail.com>",
    "message": "feat(mztab-m): add an mzTab-M data source and query layer\n\nAdd MzTabMSource(), which reads the small molecule features (SMF) of an\nmzTab-M 2.0 file and pairs them with the raw files they came from, and\nlp_mztab(), which selects the features to plot with a query such as\n\"reliability <= 2\". As MS-DIAL, MZmine and OpenMS all export mzTab-M,\nthis one source covers several tools.\n\nThe source extends ExternalDataSource. Assays are mapped to sample paths\nthrough their ms_run locations, matched by basename (and without the\nextension as a fallback). Features are annotated with the name, formula,\ndatabase identifier and reliability of the SML rows that reference them;\na feature claimed by several SML rows keeps the first and is flagged as\nambiguous. Since one compound is often reported as several adduct\nfeatures, create_compound_chromatograms() gains a key argument and the\nmzTab-M chromatograms are keyed by SMF_ID instead of name.\n\nThe vignette now plots a real example: the HUPO-PSI MTBLS263 mzTab-M file\n(Progenesis QI) with its MetaboLights raw files, cut down to eight\nfeatures and shipped in inst/extdata. tools/mztab rebuilds it. Bump the\nversion to 1.1.19.\n\nCloses #51.\n",
    "time": 1792963616
  },
